 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling, punctuation and syllables: Dò, sò and quà with their accents, \"Ah voi, Signore!\" (the libretto has A voi, signore), \"È un oretta\" with È and un sung on one note and no apostrophe (libretto un'oretta), \"dentro oscuro\" (libretto dentro scuro), \"là porta\" with an accent (libretto la porta; sung and written in IPA as the article la), \"io mene vo\" with me-ne hyphenated as one word in the print (libretto me ne), fuggia sung on two notes (libretto fuggìa; IPA fudˈdʒia, stressed on the final syllable), and the full stop printed after \"per\" in bar 97. The score repeats pietà, the lines a voi, a lei / il delitto mio non è / l'innocenza mi rubò / compatite / voi capite / nulla / questa fanciulla / che con lei girando vo / si sa, and ends with fuggia per quà four times. IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S46) and the IPA was checked against Castel. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
